  shows up in a later sweep. Practically: this spec has had my self-review and nothing else.

  [1mSelf-review found two real defects, both fixed:[0m

  1. [1mApp hostname conflated with API hostname.[0m The resolution rule said "hostname equals the staging host placeholder"
     while the only staging host in the spec was [38;5;153mstaging-api.example.com[39m — the host the app [3mcalls[0m. Detection has to
     match the host the app is [3mserved from[0m. Left as written, staging would never have resolved. The spec now defines a
     separate [38;5;153mSTAGING_HOSTNAME[39m constant (placeholder [38;5;153mstaging.example.com[39m) and says explicitly that it never appears in a
     request URL.
  2. [1m[38;5;153m?env=[39m parsing was underspecified.[0m "Contains [38;5;153menv=<name>[39m" permits substring matching, under which [38;5;153m?envelope=staging[39m
     would trip the override. Now pinned to [38;5;153mnew URLSearchParams(search).get("env")[39m, with hostname matching specified as
     exact and case-insensitive. Added two test cases to lock both down (the suite is now 9 cases, up from 7).

  I also added a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m with [38;5;153mdocs/superpowers[39m and [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers[39m, so the spec stays out of commits.

